				<main id="fsPageContent" class="fsPageContent">
							<h1 class="fsPageTitle">IPS Board Appoints Chris Bultman to District 4 Vacancy</h1>




							<div class="fsPageLayout fsLayout fsOneColumnLayout fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_62747" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class=" fsDiv fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_62748"  >

				<div class="fsElement fsPostElement fsPost  fsSingleItem" id="fsEl_62749" data-use-new="true" data-board-id="87" data-linked-element-ids="[63814]" data-selected-board="indianapolis-public-schools-news" data-overwrite-title="true" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
		
<article class="fsStyleAutoclear fsBoard-87" data-post-id="1484" data-authenticated-comments="true">

	

		
		<div class="fsTitle fsStateHidden" id="fsArticle_62749_1484">
		<a class="fsPostLink" data-slug="indianapolis-public-schools-news/post/ips-board-appoints-chris-bultman-to-district-4-vacancy" data-opens-in="element" href="https://www.myips.org/district-posts/~board/indianapolis-public-schools-news/post/ips-board-appoints-chris-bultman-to-district-4-vacancy">
			IPS Board Appoints Chris Bultman to District 4 Vacancy
</a></div>

	



		<div class="fsDateTime">
					<time datetime="2026-06-25T19:17:00-04:00" class="fsDate">
						<span class="fsMonth">Jun</span> <span class="fsDay">25</span> <span class="fsYear">2026</span>
					</time>
		</div>





		<div class="fsBody">
			<p style="line-height:1.38"><span style="font-size:12pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman',serif"><span style="color:#000000"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">The Indianapolis Public Schools (IPS) Board of School Commissioners appointed Chris Bultman on Thursday, June 25, to fill the District 4 vacancy.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size:12pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman',serif"><span style="color:#000000"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">He was selected over Lindsey Cornett, a writer and editor for congregation engagement at Englewood Community Development Corporation.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size:12pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman',serif"><span style="color:#000000"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">Bultman currently serves as regional director of external affairs for Concept Schools, a nonprofit charter management organization that supports the Indiana Math and Science Academies. His professional background includes experience as a teacher and member of the school culture team, where he worked closely with students facing challenges both inside and outside the classroom.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size:12pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman',serif"><span style="color:#000000"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">During a question-and-answer session with commissioners on June 24, he identified several priorities for the district, including improving student achievement, strengthening enrollment, supporting the district&#39;s financial health, and ensuring IPS remains a destination district for families.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size:12pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman',serif"><span style="color:#000000"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">He also emphasized the importance of collaboration across the public education landscape to better serve students and communities.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size:12pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman',serif"><span style="color:#000000"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">Bultman succeeds former Commissioner Allissa Impink, who resigned earlier this month after winning the Democratic primary for Indiana State Senate District 46.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size:12pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman',serif"><span style="color:#000000"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">He will serve in the District 4 seat through Dec. 31, 2026. In accordance with Indiana law, the District 4 seat will appear on the November 2026 ballot. The candidate elected in that election will assume office on Jan. 1, 2027.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p><span style="font-size:12pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman',serif"><span style="color:#000000"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">District 4 represents the southwest portion of the IPS district.</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

		</div>



</article>


	</div>


	</div>
	
